398
00:35:27,863 --> 00:35:33,343
なんかね、ぺこら先輩のライブにも出たし、とわのライブにも出て
You know, I appeared in Pekora-senpai's live, and Towa's live too,

399
00:35:33,343 --> 00:35:34,943
3回目よ。
so this is my third time.

400
00:35:34,943 --> 00:35:35,423
え、なにご？
Huh, what number?

401
00:35:35,423 --> 00:35:38,583
え、だから、7月5日、8月5日でペポと急におつまとびして、
Uh, so, July 5th and August 5th, Peko and I suddenly got together—

402
00:35:38,583 --> 00:35:39,323
集まったね！
We did get together!

403
00:35:39,443 --> 00:35:40,103
確かね。
That's right.

404
00:35:40,243 --> 00:35:43,583
じゃ、次の記念日の人、はい。
Now, the person with the next anniversary, yes.

405
00:35:43,983 --> 00:35:44,883
はーい！
Here!

406
00:35:44,963 --> 00:35:46,483
とわ！1月3日！
Towa! January 3rd!

407
00:35:46,683 --> 00:35:48,123
1月12…あ、1月だ！
January 12— Ah, January!

408
00:35:50,143 --> 00:35:52,563
えーっと、9月なんだけ…
Um, September, but...

409
00:35:52,943 --> 00:35:59,363
じゃ、9月は、どうかな？最終号できるかな？
Well, September, I wonder? Can we do a final issue?

410
00:35:59,363 --> 00:35:59,863
確かに。
True.

411
00:36:00,343 --> 00:36:01,963
じゃ、よいおって感じ？
Like, "Have a good year" vibe?

412
00:36:02,103 --> 00:36:02,723
よいお年？
Have a good year?

413
00:36:02,843 --> 00:36:04,863
え、もしかしてそれまで集まんないてこと？
Wait, does that mean we won't meet until then?

414
00:36:05,423 --> 00:36:08,823
なんか最近ちょっとだって、ライブばっかぺこどくろす…
Lately, it's just been live after live...

415
00:36:08,823 --> 00:36:09,783
ライブしか集まらん！
We only get together for lives!

416
00:36:10,003 --> 00:36:13,963
ペポっとライブでしか集まらない説
The theory that we only gather for lives!

417
00:36:15,203 --> 00:36:19,563
えー、でもまあ、あの、じゃあ来年もよいお年をということで、はい。
Um, but well, then have a good year for next year too, yes.

418
00:36:19,943 --> 00:36:21,283
よいお年を！早い早い！
Have a good year! Way too early!

419
00:36:21,583 --> 00:36:22,223
本当に来るの？
Are you really coming?

420
00:36:22,223 --> 00:36:22,723
うん。
Yeah.

421
00:36:22,903 --> 00:36:23,843
帰るか。
Time to go home.

422
00:36:24,023 --> 00:36:25,323
帰ろう。早い早い。
Let's go home. Way too early.

423
00:36:25,323 --> 00:36:31,763
たらりよ、たらりよ…
Tarariyo, tarariyo...

424
00:36:50,213 --> 00:36:53,563
unlasting 作詞:LiSA 作曲:草野華余子
unlasting / Lyrics: LiSA / Music: Kayoko Kusano

425
00:37:02,663 --> 00:37:11,113
一人きりでも平気とこぼれ落ちた強がり
An empty assurance escapes my lips, pretending I'll be fine by myself.

426
00:37:19,213 --> 00:37:25,263
二人の眩しすぎた日がこんなに悲しい
Those days when the two of us shone too bright now bring me so much sorrow.

427
00:37:25,613 --> 00:37:30,913
一人で生きられるなら誰かを愛したりしないから
If I was capable of living life all alone, I never would have loved in the first place.

428
00:37:48,263 --> 00:37:56,163
あなたの香り あなたの話し方
Your scent, the way you speak—

429
00:37:56,813 --> 00:38:03,763
今も身体中に“愛のカケラ”が残ってるよ
"Fragments of love" still remain all over my body.

430
00:38:04,413 --> 00:38:12,763
私の願い 私の願いはただ…
My wish, my only wish is...

431
00:38:13,763 --> 00:38:24,763
どうか貴方もどこかで泣いていますように
That you, wherever you are, are crying too.

432
00:38:40,113 --> 00:38:46,463
いつも新しい一歩は重くて寂しい
The first step of something new is always heavy and lonely.

433
00:38:51,963 --> 00:38:59,763
もし生まれ変わってももう一度あなたに出逢いたい
Even if I were born again, I'd want to meet you once more.

434
00:39:09,663 --> 00:39:16,263
真夏の日差しの真冬の白い雪
Midsummer sunlight and midwinter white snow—

435
00:39:16,663 --> 00:39:23,763
巡る季節中に“愛のカケラ”が舞い落ちて
"Fragments of love" flutter down through the turning seasons.

436
00:39:24,413 --> 00:39:32,913
幸せなのにどこかで寂しいのは
The reason why I'm happy yet feel so lonely somewhere inside

437
00:39:33,663 --> 00:39:45,313
貴方よりも大きな私の愛のせい
is because my love for you is greater than yours.

438
00:39:59,763 --> 00:40:02,763
鍵はあなたが持ったまま
You still hold the key.

439
00:40:01,790 --> 00:40:04,820
一人きりでも
Even if I am on my own,

440
00:40:04,820 --> 00:40:08,340
平気とこぼれ落ちた強がり
the pretense of strength just spills right out.

441
00:40:09,180 --> 00:40:15,000
二人の眩しすぎた日が こんなに悲しい
To think the days we shone together could be so sad...

442
00:40:16,100 --> 00:40:19,940
一人で生きられるなら
If I could live alone,

443
00:40:19,940 --> 00:40:24,790
誰かを愛したりしないから
I wouldn't have to love anyone else.

444
00:40:25,570 --> 00:40:28,250
あなたの香り あなたの話し方
Your scent and the way you talk—

445
00:40:28,250 --> 00:40:32,640
今も身体中に“愛のカケラ”が残ってるよ
even now, fragments of love remain inside me.

446
00:40:34,860 --> 00:40:41,620
私の願い 私の願いはただ…
My only wish, my only wish is simply...

447
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:50,580
どうか あなたが幸せでありますように
that somewhere, you are crying, too, and are happy.

448
00:41:03,080 --> 00:41:10,830
いつも新しい一歩は 重くて寂しい
Every new step I take is so heavy and lonely.

449
00:41:12,220 --> 00:41:19,090
もし生まれ変わっても もう一度あなたに出会いたい
If I were reborn, I'd want to meet you once again.

450
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:26,810
真夏の日差し 真冬の白い雪
Midsummer sunshine, midwinter white snow.

451
00:41:26,810 --> 00:41:35,704
巡る季節の中に…
In the turning seasons...

452
00:41:52,514 --> 00:42:01,094
空飛ぶ羽根と引き換えに 繋ぎ合う手を選んだ僕ら
We chose hands to hold instead of wings to fly through the sky.

453
00:42:01,094 --> 00:42:05,794
それでも空に魅せられて 夢を重ねるのは罪か
Even so, fascinated by the sky, is dreaming a sin?

454
00:42:06,694 --> 00:42:11,434
夏は秋の背中を見て その顔を思い浮かべる
Summer watches autumn's back, picturing its face.

455
00:42:11,434 --> 00:42:15,984
憧れなのか 恋なのか 叶わぬと知りながら
Is it longing? Is it love? Knowing it won't come true.

456
00:42:15,984 --> 00:42:21,164
重力が眠りにつく 1000年に一度の今日
On this millennium-once-in-a-lifetime day when gravity falls asleep,

457
00:42:21,164 --> 00:42:28,244
太陽の死角に立ち 僕らこの星を出よう
let's stand in the sun's blind spot and leave this star.

458
00:42:29,264 --> 00:42:35,264
彼が目を覚ました時 連れ戻せない場所へ
To a place we can't return once he wakes his eyes.

459
00:42:35,264 --> 00:42:40,894
「せーの」で大地を蹴って ここではない星へ行こう
On three, let's kick the earth and go to another star!

460
00:42:44,854 --> 00:42:48,034
もう少しで運命の向こう
Just a little more beyond fate.

461
00:42:48,034 --> 00:42:50,904
もう少しで文明の向こう
Just a little more beyond civilization.

462
00:42:50,904 --> 00:42:54,184
もう少しで運命の向こう
Just a little more beyond fate.

463
00:42:54,184 --> 00:42:56,154
もう少しで…
Just a little more...

464
00:42:56,374 --> 00:43:01,804
夢に僕らで帆を張って 来るべき日のために夜を越え
We'll hoist our sails with dreams, crossing the night for the days to come.

465
00:43:01,804 --> 00:43:08,334
いざ期待だけ満タンで あとはどうにかなるさと肩を組んだ
Full of expectations, arms linked, whatever happens will happen.

466
00:43:08,334 --> 00:43:13,094
怖くないわけない でも 止まらない
It's not that we aren't scared, but we won't stop.

467
00:43:13,094 --> 00:43:17,844
ピンチの先回りしたって 僕らしようがないから
Even if trouble looms ahead, we have no other choice.

468
00:43:17,844 --> 00:43:22,754
僕らの恋が言う 声が言う
Our love speaks, our voice speaks:

469
00:43:22,754 --> 00:43:25,454
「行け」と言う
"Go," it says.

